{"repositoryId":1230675117,"availability":"available","full":"garancewetz/signe-astronomique","name":"signe-astronomique","description":"Cockpit web that computes your true astronomical sign — IAU 1930 constellations, equinox precession, Ophiuchus included. Cesium 3D scene, sidereal computation, live SGP4 orbital population.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-06T08:04:47Z","updated":"2026-10-19T04:16:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://signe-astronomique.netlify.app/","topics":["astrology","astronomy","celestrak","cesium","cesiumjs","constellations","iau","ophiuchus","precession","react","satellites","sgp4","sidereal-astrology","typescript","vite","webgl","zodiac"],"demo":"https://signe-astronomique.netlify.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:48.289Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:48.289Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:48.289Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:04:48.289Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A web cockpit that computes your true astronomical sign — the constellation the Sun was actually in when you were born, using IAU 1930 boundaries, equinox precession, and Ophiuchus as the 13th sign.","Mainstream astrology uses the tropical zodiac, a fiction frozen 2000 years ago. Because of equinox precession, your tropical \"sign\" no longer matches the constellation the Sun was in when you were born. This project does the actual sidereal computation — RA/Dec in J2000, then epoch correction — and projects the Sun's position onto the IAU 1930 constellation boundaries. Most people end up with a different sign than their horoscope, and many fall into Ophiuchus."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/garancewetz/signe-astronomique/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"968fba613675cd054b50daf378ab74863cb85881f99796c751a64f54b337334b","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:04:48.386Z"},"over